CHAPTER 1
The Long Night

    We are such stuff as dreams are made on.
        -- William Shakespeare, The Tempest

The rain had been falling for three days.

Maria hadn't slept for two of them.

#

When the telephone finally rang, she already knew who it was.

She opened the letter:

    Dear Judith,

    I am leaving.

    Goodbye.

    Love,
    John.

The paper was dry, which somehow made it worse.[^dry]


CHAPTER 2
The House at the End

The house looked smaller in daylight.

That was the first thing Judith thought when she saw it again: not abandoned, not sinister, not even particularly old. Just _smaller_.

SECTION
The Door

Memory has a habit of rebuilding rooms to fit the things we are afraid to find inside them.

She put the key into the lock.

[^dry]: Notes can live anywhere in a Feather file and are collected at the end of the reading unit that references them.
